<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Said Mohamed Cheikh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1904–1970</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Said Mohamed Cheikh was a Comorian politician who led the islands' government under French rule. When the Territory of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comoro-islands">Comoros</a> gained internal autonomy in 1961 he became head of its government council, holding the post until his death in 1970. His period in office saw the capital moved from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzaoudzi">Dzaoudzi</a> on Mayotte to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moroni">Moroni</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grande-comore">Grande Comore</a>, a decision long resented on Mayotte.</p></div>
